# @colyseus/core holds process-wide singleton state (the matchmaker's room
# registry). Several @colyseus/* packages have a circular *optional* peer
# dependency on it (@colyseus/core <-> @colyseus/auth), which makes pnpm's
# strict, per-consumer peer resolution create two physically distinct copies
# of @colyseus/core in node_modules/.pnpm — one for each resolution context.
# Two copies means two separate in-memory room registries, so a seat reserved
# via one copy is invisible to the other: every WebSocket join then fails with
# "seat reservation expired" even though the HTTP matchmake call just
# succeeded. See docs/adr/0002-networking.md.
#
# Hoisting every @colyseus/* package to the top-level node_modules/ guarantees
# a single physical copy, which Node's normal resolution then finds for every
# consumer regardless of which require() chain asks for it.
public-hoist-pattern[]=@colyseus/*
